{"id":"world-2010-vs2010","known":"2010-04-12","occurred":"2010-04-12","kind":"tech","stage":"effective","title":"Visual Studio 2010 becomes available","impact":"Adds .NET Framework 4 and drops the bundled Crystal Reports, so report projects need a separate runtime; older solutions are converted when opened","industries":["*"],"areas":["platform"],"tech":{"product":"visualstudio","version":"2010","markers":[{"lang":"sln","name":"solution format 11.00","pattern":"(?m)^﻿?Microsoft Visual Studio Solution File, Format Version 11\\.00\\b"},{"lang":"sln","name":"Visual Studio 2010 comment line","pattern":"(?m)^# Visual (Studio|C# Express|Basic Express) 2010\\b"},{"lang":"proj","name":"MSBuild ToolsVersion 4.0","pattern":"\\bToolsVersion\\s*=\\s*\"4\\.0\""}]},"sources":["https://news.microsoft.com/source/2010/04/11/microsoft-visual-studio-2010-and-microsoft-net-framework-4-available/","https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/extensibility/internals/solution-dot-sln-file","https://blogs.windows.com/windowsexperience/2010/04/12/availability-of-visual-studio-2010-net-framework-4-announced/"],"status":"unverified"}
